# REGRESSION PIN — indirect-call `&`-param ABI, TYPE axis cell: **16-byte
# non-resource struct** (`struct{int,int}`), through an ANNOTATED LOCAL
# `Callable`. Sibling of `callable_local_struct_amp_param_segv.gg` (8B cell).
#
# WHY IT LIVES IN known_gaps/: `runtime_parity_corpus` (tests/integration.rs)
# reads only `tests/fixtures/*.gg` and never descends subdirectories, so this
# net asserts fully on C AND LLVM through its LIVE test while adding ZERO
# self-host parity-corpus inflow. The self-host lane still MIS-LOWERS this
# shape (measured below), so a top-level placement would be new parity debt.
#
# RED-VERIFIED against the PRE-fix compiler (`git checkout -- src && cargo build`,
# then re-run — reverting a patch does NOT rebuild):
#     C    -> rc 139 (SIGSEGV), no output
#     LLVM -> rc 139 (SIGSEGV), no output
# POST-fix both backends print `2` / `4`.
#
# LANE AXIS (measured with the self-host driver, `--emit-c` -> cc -> run):
#     self-host -> rc 139. The SH lane has its OWN indirect-call ABI defect
#     (it never forms the pointer at all); filed separately in TODO.md.
#
# INTENDED: the callee writes through the `&`, so `2` then `4`.
struct Q:
    int a
    int b

void bump(Q &q):
    q.a = q.a + 1
    q.b = q.b + 2

int main():
    Callable[void(Q &)] f = bump
    Q q = Q(1, 2)
    f(&q)
    print(q.a)
    print(q.b)
    return 0
